# The adhan recording is a copyrighted recitation supplied by the user,
# not something with confirmed rights to redistribute publicly. It's
# deployed directly on the server (and can live here locally too) but is
# deliberately kept out of git history so the public GitHub repo doesn't
# distribute it. See CHANGELOG.md for the full story.
adhan.mp3

# Generated on the server every ~10s by a systemd timer (see
# ARCHITECTURE.md's server health section), never authored by hand or
# tracked in git — same reasoning as adhan.mp3: this is server state,
# not app code, and a deploy must never overwrite or delete the live
# one (also excluded from the rsync in .github/workflows/deploy.yml).
server-stats.json

# Written by the deploy workflow itself right after a successful
# rsync — same server-state reasoning as server-stats.json above, and
# also excluded from the rsync so a deploy never wipes the very
# timestamp it just wrote.
.last-successful-deploy

# macOS Finder metadata — not authored, not app code, shouldn't be
# committed just because Finder happened to browse this folder.
.DS_Store
